{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":10058792,"ns":0,"title":"Backlash (engineering)","extract":"In mechanical engineering, backlash, sometimes called lash, play, or slop, is a clearance or lost motion in a mechanism caused by gaps between the parts. It can be defined as \"the maximum distance or angle through which any part of a mechanical system may be moved in one direction without applying appreciable force or motion to the next part in mechanical sequence.\"p.","description":"Clearance between mating components","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}